2.1 Ptolemy Miniconference

On Friday, March 14, we held a full day miniconference that reviewed
the Ptolemy project.  The objectives of the conference were primarily
to report to and solicit advice from the industrial sponsors and friends
of the project.  The miniconference reviewed both this DARPA effort, and
our other DARPA effort entitled "System-Level Design Methodology for
Embedded Signal Processors." That project is wrapping up and will
conclude with the release of Ptolemy 0.7.  Thus, the more mature
results presented at the miniconference stem from that project, while
the more forward-looking presentations focused on this one.
The conference included several outside speakers reporting on uses
